§ `ss 7, 8 -- a public health service in a public hospital`

-- k090, c060: the stroke unit and the maternity service are run by a WA health service provider.
#ASSERT `Is my care a public health service` `a health service provider` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my care a public health service` `a contracted health entity under a contract with a health service provider or the State` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my care a public health service` `a private provider with no such contract` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my care a public health service` `a health service provider` FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Is the hospital a public hospital` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the hospital a public hospital` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `s 55(1) -- may the hospital charge me at all`

-- The Act lets the provider charge unless the National Health Agreement (in force) or a s 56(2)(b) order says not.
#ASSERT `May the hospital charge me at all` `a health service provider` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the hospital charge me at all` `a health service provider` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the hospital charge me at all` `a health service provider` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May the hospital charge me at all` `a health service provider` FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§ `Order cll 3A, 6A, 11-15 -- what class of patient am I`

-- c060: antenatal clinic visits as an out-patient, the birth as a public in-patient. k090: the stroke admission.
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `Chloe at 26, a Medicare-eligible public patient (c060)` `as an out-patient` EQUALS `an eligible out-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `Chloe at 26, a Medicare-eligible public patient (c060)` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `a public in-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `Chloe at 26, electing to be a private patient (c060 compared)` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `a private in-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `Jake at 56 after the stroke, a public patient (k090)` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `a public in-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `a visitor who is not Medicare-eligible` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `an ineligible in-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `an asylum seeker awaiting a protection visa, not Medicare-eligible` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `not classified: no fees or charges are payable (cl 6A)`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `an involuntary patient, not Medicare-eligible, for other treatment` `as an out-patient` EQUALS `an ineligible out-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `a visitor, not Medicare-eligible, with a damages claim` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `a compensable in-patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `a visitor, not Medicare-eligible, with a damages claim` `as a same day patient` EQUALS `an ineligible same day patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `a Medicare-eligible nursing home type patient electing private` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `a nursing home type private patient`
#ASSERT `What class of patient am I` `a person declared not eligible under s 6(2) of the Health Insurance Act` `as an in-patient` EQUALS `not classified: the Order gives no in-patient class`

-- cl 3A(4)(a): a compensable same day patient must be Medicare-eligible; the in-patient class has no such condition.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a compensable patient` `a visitor, not Medicare-eligible, with a damages claim` `as a same day patient`)
#ASSERT `Am I a compensable patient` `an injured worker under workers compensation` `as an out-patient`

#ASSERT `Am I free of all fees under cl 6A` `an involuntary patient, not Medicare-eligible, for Mental Health Act treatment` `as an in-patient`
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I free of all fees under cl 6A` `an asylum seeker who is Medicare-eligible` `as an in-patient`)

§ `Order cll 5, 6; Schedule 1 Divisions 1, 2 -- what the hospital charges me per day`

-- c060: the birth as a public in-patient costs Chloe nothing; electing private, $467 a day in a shared ward, at most
-- $774 in a single room she asked for. k090: Jake's three weeks as a public in-patient cost nothing.
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `Chloe at 26, a Medicare-eligible public patient (c060)` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS `nothing to pay`
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `Chloe at 26, electing to be a private patient (c060 compared)` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS (`a fixed charge of` 467)
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `Chloe at 26, electing to be a private patient (c060 compared)` `as an in-patient` TRUE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS (`a charge of no more than` 774)
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `Jake at 56 after the stroke, a public patient (k090)` `as an in-patient` TRUE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS `nothing to pay`
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `a visitor who is not Medicare-eligible` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS (`a fixed charge of` 3417)
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `a Medicare-eligible nursing home type patient` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS (`a fixed charge of` 82.50)
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `a road-crash patient under third party insurance` `as an in-patient` FALSE `a hospital bed, ventilator dependent with tracheostomy and 24-hour individual care` EQUALS `nothing to pay`
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `a patient with a damages claim` `as an in-patient` FALSE `a hospital bed, with 24-hour care for airway management` EQUALS (`a fixed charge of` 4305)
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `a patient with a damages claim` `as a same day patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS (`a fixed charge of` 4465)
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `a visitor who is not Medicare-eligible` `as a day patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS `not fixed by the Order`
#ASSERT `What does the hospital charge me per day` `Chloe at 26, a Medicare-eligible public patient (c060)` `as an out-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` EQUALS `per service instead`

-- k090: 21 days. As a public in-patient, nothing; had he elected private, 21 x $467 = $9,807; not Medicare-eligible,
-- 21 x $3,417 = $71,757.
#ASSERT `What will my stay cost under the Order` `Jake at 56 after the stroke, a public patient (k090)` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` 21 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What will my stay cost under the Order` `Jake at 56, had he elected to be a private patient (k090 compared)` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` 21 EQUALS 9807
#ASSERT `What will my stay cost under the Order` `a visitor who is not Medicare-eligible` `as an in-patient` FALSE `an ordinary hospital bed` 21 EQUALS 71757

